Z||000000||Bill H||10-17-2000||09:17 PM|||| I have an 88 formula and need to rebuild the motor. I was thinking of using PISA's 2.8-3.1 stroking kit with a Crane Comp-u-cam.<BR>I would like near 200hp if possable and be a daily driver if I wanted too. Do any of you have any suggestions? I also know RS Motorsports in Canada makes a bolt on supercharger that is good for 80HP but I am not sure if the crank will take it. Thanks for any help||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||09:30 PM||||the easiest way to get 200 proven hp is to contact Ed Parks and get his already build 3.6 and drop it right in. not too pricey.. comes with a warranty and hes great to work with.  wecome to the forum!  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#offer" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#offer</A>   hope this helps.. and saves you a few bucks!  the s/c kits makes you ditch the A/C...<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-17-2000||10:51 PM||||There is nothing wrong with the PISA kit except I think you can find it cheaper if you shop around. I think the Fiero Store has a kit too. You can scrounge the junkyards for even better bargains. Check out this link, some good info about possible engine upgrades.<P> <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm</A> ||||reg||1
